# Shell scripts MUST stay LF — with core.autocrlf=true, a CRLF checkout breaks
# bash (Git Bash) on Windows with `$'\r': command not found` errors.
*.sh text eol=lf

# SQL MUST stay LF — several migrations rewrite live function bodies at runtime via
# pg_get_functiondef() + replace() on LF-anchored strings (e.g. the exclusion-perimeter
# guard injections). With core.autocrlf=true a CRLF checkout stores \r into prosrc, the
# LF anchor fails to match, and `supabase db reset` aborts mid-run. Keep migrations,
# pgTAP tests, and seed byte-identical to the index (which is already LF).
*.sql text eol=lf

# Markdown MUST stay LF in the repo AND the working tree — the tracker docs
# (PROGRESS.md / CLAUDE.md / archives) are read and rewritten by shell tools (awk,
# sed, node scripts, the lint:progress gate) that see raw bytes. With
# core.autocrlf=true alone, checkout produces CRLF and every session's toolchain
# sees different bytes than the repo stores — the LF/CRLF drift class this line
# retires. eol=lf overrides autocrlf for these files in both directions.
*.md text eol=lf

# The Prettier ignore file is read by node tooling and hand-edited by sessions on
# Windows; keep it LF so the working tree matches the index and git stops rewriting
# it to CRLF on every checkout (Prettier itself tolerates either).
.prettierignore text eol=lf
